#: ../../user/glossary.md:1
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:3
msgid "Key terms used throughout this documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:5
msgid "ReScript Language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md
msgid "Binding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:9
msgid ""
"A `let` declaration that associates a name with a value or function. "
"Similar to variable declaration in other languages, but bindings are "
"immutable by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:3
msgid "Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:12
msgid ""
"A namespace unit in ReScript that groups related types, values, and sub-"
"modules. Every `.res` file is implicitly a module named after the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:6
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:15
msgid ""
"A `.resi` file that declares the public API of a module. Only "
"declarations listed in the interface file are visible to other modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:9
msgid "Variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:18
msgid ""
"An algebraic data type that can hold one of several named constructors, "
"each optionally carrying data. For example, `type color = Red | Green | "
"Blue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:12
msgid "Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:21
msgid ""
"A structured data type with named fields. Fields are accessed with dot "
"notation and are immutable by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:15
msgid "Pipe Operator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:24
msgid ""
"The `->` operator that passes the result of the left expression as the "
"first argument to the function on the right. Enables readable left-to-"
"right data transformation chains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:18
msgid "Decorator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:27
msgid ""
"An `@` annotation that modifies the behavior of the following "
"declaration. Examples include `@module`, `@val`, `@send`, `@genType`, and"
" `@react.component`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:21
msgid "External"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:30
msgid ""
"An `external` declaration that binds a ReScript name to a JavaScript "
"value or function. Used for FFI (Foreign Function Interface) with "
"JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:24
msgid "JSX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:33
msgid ""
"XML-like syntax used in ReScript for building React components. ReScript "
"JSX compiles to `React.createElement` calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:27
msgid "Pattern Matching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:36
msgid ""
"A `switch` expression that destructures values and matches them against "
"patterns. More powerful than traditional switch/case — it checks "
"exhaustiveness at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:30
msgid "Type Inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:39
msgid ""
"The compiler's ability to automatically determine the type of an "
"expression without explicit type annotations. ReScript has complete type "
"inference powered by the Hindley-Milner type system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:33
msgid "PPX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:42
msgid ""
"A preprocessor extension that transforms the AST (Abstract Syntax Tree) "
"at compile time. Decorators like `@react.component` and `@deriving` are "
"implemented as PPX transformations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:36
msgid "Open Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:45
msgid ""
"An `open` declaration that brings all exports of a module into the "
"current scope, allowing you to use them without the module prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:48
msgid "IDE Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md
msgid "Intention Action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:52
msgid ""
"A context-aware code transformation available via `Alt+Enter` (or "
"`Option+Return` on macOS). Intentions suggest improvements or "
"refactorings based on the code at the cursor position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:3
msgid "Live Template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:55
msgid ""
"A code snippet that expands from an abbreviation when you press `Tab`. "
"For example, typing `letfn` and pressing `Tab` expands to a full function"
" declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:6
msgid "Postfix Completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:58
msgid ""
"A completion triggered by typing a dot suffix after an expression. For "
"example, `expr.switch` transforms the expression into a `switch` "
"statement. Unlike live templates, postfix completions wrap existing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:9
msgid "Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:61
msgid ""
"The ability to collapse code blocks (modules, functions, comments) to "
"show only their first line, making it easier to navigate large files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:12
msgid "Structure View"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:64
msgid ""
"A tool window (`Alt+7`) that displays a tree outline of declarations in "
"the current file — modules, functions, types, and externals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:15
msgid "Code Lens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:67
msgid ""
"Inline annotations displayed above function declarations showing their "
"inferred type signatures. Powered by the CodeVision API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:18
msgid "Inlay Hint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:70
msgid ""
"A small inline label displayed in the editor showing type information for"
" variables and parameters. Provided by the Language Server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:21
msgid "Code Inspection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:73
msgid ""
"An automated code quality check that runs in the background and "
"highlights potential issues with warnings or suggestions. Available "
"inspections can be configured in Settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:24
msgid "Quick Fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:76
msgid ""
"An automatic correction for a detected issue, offered in the context menu"
" or via `Alt+Enter`. Quick fixes are typically paired with inspections or"
" compiler diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:27
msgid "Surround With"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A feature (`Ctrl+Alt+T`) that wraps selected code with a control "
"structure such as `if`, `switch`, `try`, or a block `{}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:30
msgid "Run Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:82
msgid ""
"A saved set of parameters for executing a task — such as building a "
"ReScript project, running tests, or debugging compiled JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:33
msgid "Error Lens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:85
msgid ""
"Inline diagnostic messages displayed at the end of each line in the "
"editor, showing errors and warnings without hovering. Color-coded by "
"severity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:88
msgid "Plugin Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md
msgid "LSP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:92
msgid ""
"Language Server Protocol. A standardized JSON-RPC protocol for "
"communication between an IDE (client) and a language-specific server that"
" provides semantic features like completion, diagnostics, and navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:3
msgid "Language Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:95
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The `@rescript/language-server` process that runs in the background, "
"analyzing your ReScript project and providing semantic features to the "
"plugin via {term}`LSP`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:6
msgid "Native Feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:98
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A feature implemented directly in the plugin using JFlex lexer and "
"IntelliJ Platform APIs. Native features work without the {term}`Language "
"Server` — for example, syntax highlighting, code folding, and brace "
"matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:9
msgid "Semantic Token"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A token classification provided by the {term}`Language Server` that "
"carries semantic meaning (e.g., \"this identifier is a type\" or \"this "
"is a namespace\"). Enables more accurate highlighting than lexer-based "
"tokenization alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:12
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:104
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Errors, warnings, and informational messages reported by the "
"{term}`Language Server` and displayed inline in the editor. Diagnostics "
"update as you edit the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:15
msgid "PSI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:107
msgid ""
"Program Structure Interface. IntelliJ Platform's in-memory representation"
" of source code as a tree of typed elements. The plugin's lexer and "
"parser build PSI trees that power navigation, structure view, and "
"refactoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:18
msgid "Stub Index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/glossary.md:110
msgid ""
"A persistent, file-based index of declaration signatures (names, types, "
"modules) extracted from PSI stubs. Enables fast symbol search across the "
"entire project without parsing every file."
msgstr ""

